Patch 0078: the rest of the IOP thread, on top of 0077 (off by default: DON_IOP_THREAD=1 enables it).
What it adds to the worker that 0077 introduced: the thread is named "IopThread"; DON_IOP_STRESS_US=<n> makes it sleep
0..n us (random, time-seeded) before each slice, to prove the result does not depend on host timing (off by default, no
cost when off); and the SPU2 hooks: the library allows every call but the host pull only from the thread that opened
it, so IopHostSpu2 gains optional thread_begin/thread_end, called by the worker (the host sets them in
src/host/spu2_glue.cpp), and the host adapter (ps2_iop_host.*) is completed for calls that come from the worker
(audioCommand/memoryCard/allocateGuest/freeGuest refuse and log if they are ever reached from it).
Design (all of it, 0077 + 0078): the IOP runs slice N (one EE batch, 2048 EE cycles) while the EE runs slice N+1; what the
IOP does to the EE (writeGuest, zeroGuest, sendSifCommand) is queued while it runs on the worker and applied in order by
the EE thread at the next boundary and at every EE->IOP entry, so the result depends on emulated cycles only.
Verified: perf_fight.py with DON_IOP_THREAD=1 reached 7800 blanks with the same state hash as the inline path (once);
GameThread 17.83 -> ~10.5 ms per blank.
NOT verified yet: that two runs give the same hash; a run with the stress delay; that the SPU2 hook is free of races
with the host audio side. Original work, GPL-3.0.

